{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381964-fresh-necromancer-character-concepts","id":1381964,"title":"Fresh \"necromancer\" character concepts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-16T13:06:01-07:00","id":1381964,"title":"Fresh \"necromancer\" character concepts?","content":"Please throw me some fresh ideas for Death-focused Moros that would make for interesting storyteller characters.<br /> <br /> I need to flesh out a couple of pentacle mages for a chronicle and I'm having a lot trouble getting past the standard tropes. I'd like to throw some characters at my players that feel novel, but my creativity is failing me. This is a &quot;world building&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I think the cornerstone would be Death-centric obsessions that can help drive their behavior and goals.<br /> <br /> These two characters need to be related to one another somehow, like master/apprentice,in the same cabal, feuding with each other, etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-16-2020, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T13:50:05-07:00","id":1381972,"title":"","content":"Have you ever heard of the crystal sage ? No, of course not, all mentions of him must be in the Censorea by now.<br /> <br /> The sage would seek out the best of their field. The greatest artists, the most innovative engineers, the most masterful athletes, etc. He would wait until their talents hit their apex before murdering them.<br /> <br /> But it would not end there, oh no. For he would tear their souls and trap them in platonic crystal matrices. In his Sanctum he would weave them into a forest of crystalline neurons. Shaping them into an gestalt of spirits.<br /> <br /> His apprentice was a researcher of artificial bodies. Always testing how to grant ghosts bodies evolved with perfected metals, ancient clockwork mechanisms (Infrastructure) and Artifacts of the Time Before.<br /> <br /> Legend has it that they were close to locating the body of Talos. These madmen planned to have a Supernal being infuse the soul circuit into Atlantean Dragon Bone, transmuting it into the most powerful soul stone of all time. By using it to power Talos, they would create a man made god to oppose the Exarchs. <br /> <br /> At least so was the theory. The Pentacle raided their Sanctum before it could happen, terminated both of them and seized the notes. <br /> <br /> We thought the matter ended. But last month we found victims with signs that matched their killing pattern. When we exhumed the bodies, all we found were the crumbling remains of the most lifelike mechanical wraiths we had ever seen....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-16-2020, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T14:15:04-07:00","id":1381975,"title":"","content":"Guardian of the Veil manages a network of Ghosts who steal memories of supernatural events. However, he gets increasingly more distracted by analysing the effect of different memories on his charges. Some of the Ghosts are undergoing shifts in personality as they get more overburdened.<br /> <br /> Thearch studies how Ceremonies of hedge practicioners are able to interact with Ghosts, corpses and other deathly phenomena. She alters the variables of Ceremonies with her Supernal magic to see how she can influence their outcomes. So far, her Shielding magic prevented any major harm.<br /> <br /> Thearch is organizing a group to raid the Underworld for Dissonance-free resources for their Order's Cryptopolies. They don't care about the disruption they cause to that environment. They're currently studying how to turn Ghosts into life-extending medicine, even though Ladder management worries that such could interfere with Awakenings.<br /> <br /> Mystagogue studies all sorts of undead to see how their natures interact with Pancryptia. He suspects that their attunement to Death may erase signs of their passing, like the &quot;Without a Trace&quot; spell. He's currently fascinated by how difficult Vampires are to catch on camera.<br /> <br /> Mystagogue runs a black market of cadavers. She sells body parts for transplants and sacraments, perfected leather and bones for magic, and miscellaneous leftovers as monster food. The Ministry of Mammon are increasingly frustrated by having her as competition.<br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrow started by weaponizing zombies. Now he uses creative taxidermy and embalming to create undead chimeras, big and small. He wants to recreate a hungry monstrosity he and his Order once destroyed.<br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrow styles herself as a mythical psychopomp, escorting Ghosts from Upper Reaches to a Dominion of their preference. She has to fight spiteful Ghosts, Chtonians and all kinds of bizarre Underworld phenomena.<br /> <br /> Free Councillor collects bodies of people in coma and enables his Ghost friends to Claim them. The undead are vouched for and trustworthy, but the sloppy coverup got Sleeper investigators on his trail. It's only a matter of time until Hunters notice.<br /> <br /> Free Councilor wants to create a comprehensive archive of Soul Marks caused by different kinds of near death experiences, in order to aid psychological treatment. She doesn't know the Consillium is suspecting her of being a Reaper.<br /> <br /> Free Councillor routinely summons a Supernal Entity to resurrect people without risk of further Dissonance. He addresses the problem of Soullessness by summoning the subject's Astral Walker and letting them inhabit the body. She currently seeks a replacement that doesn't make her patients so obsessive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T16:44:43-07:00","id":1382011,"title":"","content":"Holy cow! Thanks guys. Lots of inspiration there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:53:53-07:00","id":1393426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381964-fresh-necromancer-character-concepts?p=1381972#post1381972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We thought the matter ended. But last month we found victims with signs that matched their killing pattern. When we exhumed the bodies, all we found were the crumbling remains of the most lifelike mechanical wraiths we had ever seen....</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to give a shout-out to Kaiser. I ran a three-session story around this idea (also drawing on inspiration from an old Star Wars novel &quot;Truce at Bakura&quot; that has a similar idea). We had a lot of fun with this. The stories are part of a &quot;prequel&quot; series set 10 years prior to my &quot;main event&quot; chronicle so that my players feel hooked in with the Consilium where it's going to be set without a lot of raw exposition.<br /> <br /> I also caught hints that Kaiser was pulling in inspiration from Elder Scrolls (the Numidium) and that keyed off some other ideas I can work in too. Thanks Kaiser!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:39:22-07:00","id":1393436,"title":"","content":"I have been found out. The inspiration was partially from Numidium, but also from the Infinity Circuit of the Aeldari. The return of the killer was inspired from The Harvester quest from Deus Ex: Mankind Divided.<br /> <br /> I am happy to hear everyone had fun with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T00:28:40-07:00","id":1394513,"title":"","content":"Tiresias: Mysterium mage focused on lost knowledge. He travels the globe seeking means to summon ghosts from the past to question them. He's Obsessed with dead natural languages as they were when they were living, and is also obsessed in finding secret histories..<br /> <br /> He started out far more optimistic than he's become; one of the unchanging facts throughout time is that human beings are bastards. Beautiful peoples are a lot nicer when described in flattering ways than when you find out about their actual murders and pettiness. It hasn't occurred to him, yet, to consider how significant the biases from using ghosts might be.<br /> <br /> An Adamantine Arrow Obrimos who went by the handle &quot;Raven&quot; has accompanied his searching many times. He shifted his shadow name to Odysseus shortly after Tiresias agreed to start teaching him Death. He's focusing on Prime and Death, right now, as a means for fighting things that are intangible and conjuring weapons at need.. an Obsession of his..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}